@@ -0,0 +1,1076 @@
+"""SDMA copy engines for symm_mem's fused all-gather + matmul and matmul + reduce-scatter on ROCm,
+and their scaled (_scaled_mm) variants.
+
+The default implementations move shards with tensor copies from peers'
+symmetric-memory buffers (_pipelined_all_gather_and_consume,
+_pipelined_produce_and_all2all). On ROCm, HIP runs concurrent copies out of those
+buffers one at a time, so the all-gather moves at about one link's rate, and the
+copies compete with the matmuls for compute units. Here every rank pushes its
+data into each peer's inbox with ROCr's
+hsa_amd_memory_async_copy_on_engine, one SDMA engine per peer (the engine ROCr
+prefers for writing to that peer), all peers at once. The copies use no compute
+units.
+
+All-gather + matmul: each rank's rows are cut into `chunks` pieces. Piece c of
+rank r lands in rows r * M + c * block of every peer's inbox, so the inbox holds
+the gathered A in natural order. The compute stream waits for piece c of every
+rank and runs its matmul, one batched GEMM over the (world, block, K) rows, while
+later pieces are in flight. The scaled variant runs one _scaled_mm per rank's
+piece; row-wise sharded A scales travel with A's rows, in the same pushes.
+
+Matmul + reduce-scatter: matmul c computes this rank's partial sums for piece c of
+every rank's output rows; once it is done, the engines push each owner's piece
+into that owner's inbox, and each rank sums the partials it received for piece c
+(in fp32) one piece behind, so the next matmul is never held up by a wait. The
+scaled variant computes the partial sums with one _scaled_mm per owner, in its
+output dtype.
+
+Each piece's GEMMs are the same for every call of a shape, and so are the order
+of the copies and the order of the fp32 sums, so results are bitwise
+reproducible from run to run.
+
+Each call zeroes its flags and puts this rank's own data in place on the compute
+stream, then passes a barrier; a one-thread kernel then releases the copies,
+which wait for it on the SDMA engines.
+
+Inbox (TORCH_SYMM_MEM_ROCM_SDMA_INBOX): with ipc (default), each rank's inbox is
+device memory that the other ranks' processes map with hipIpc handles, and the
+barrier is a one-thread kernel on arrival words mapped the same way, bounded
+like a flag wait; this path never rendezvouses symmetric memory. With symm_mem,
+the inbox is the group's symmetric-memory workspace (get_symm_mem_workspace) and
+the barrier its signal-pad barrier. An ipc inbox grows like the workspace, and
+the memory it outgrew stays mapped for as long as the process runs, as graphs
+captured earlier may still use it.
+
+Failures: no wait, on the GPU or the host, is unbounded. A flag wait records
+which flags did not land within TORCH_SYMM_MEM_ROCM_SDMA_TIMEOUT_S seconds
+(default 30), and the stream moves on (that call's output is wrong; the call's
+later waits return at once). Waiting for a slot's previous copies before reusing
+it is bounded by the same timeout, and a barrier by three times it (an ipc
+barrier that runs out of time is reported like a flag wait; a symm_mem one
+faults the GPU). With
+TORCH_SYMM_MEM_ROCM_SDMA_ON_TIMEOUT=abort (default) a watchdog thread logs the
+failure and aborts the process within about 0.1 s; with =raise the next eager
+call raises.
+
+A process never leaves copies waiting on its GPU's SDMA engines: when an
+exception (including KeyboardInterrupt) stops an eager call after its copies
+were issued, before the watchdog aborts, at exit, and on SIGTERM (a handler set
+up with the transport, which then runs the previous disposition), the transport
+drains: every copy is released and given DRAIN_S seconds to finish, and the
+flag writes still to come carry a value that tells peers the call was abandoned,
+so their waits fail at once rather than at the timeout. After an exception the
+rank still passes the call's last barrier, so peers are not left to time out
+there, and the error is raised; if the copies did not finish, later calls raise
+too.
+
+CUDA graphs: a call captured into a graph enqueues its host side (arming its
+signals and issuing its copies) as a host-function node, so every replay issues
+the copies when the stream reaches the call. Captured calls take their signals
+from slots apart from eager calls', so an eager call never waits on a graph's
+copies or the reverse. As for the other symm_mem ops, the inbox cannot be
+allocated during capture: run each op once, eagerly, with the shapes it will be
+captured with (the first call per process group also sets up this module).
+
+Opt-in with TORCH_SYMM_MEM_ENABLE_ROCM_SDMA=1. The transport (_rocm_sdma.hip) is
+built with torch.utils.cpp_extension on first use, for the GPU's architecture
+(needs hipcc). It runs on the architectures in VALIDATED_ARCHS; on others the
+default path runs unless TORCH_SYMM_MEM_ROCM_SDMA_ALLOW_UNTESTED=1. Pieces per
+rank: TORCH_SYMM_MEM_ROCM_SDMA_CHUNKS, or by default the most pieces, up to
+AUTO_MAX_CHUNKS, that keep each piece at least AUTO_MIN_PIECE_BYTES (a piece of the
+rank's A rows for the all-gather, of an owner's output rows for the reduce-scatter),
+taking a power of two; then the largest count not above that which divides the rows.
+Smaller pieces start the first GEMM sooner but give the engines and the GEMMs less
+work per launch.
+"""
+
+import atexit
+import ctypes
+import hashlib
+import logging
+import math
+import os
+import sys
+import threading
+import time
+from pathlib import Path
+
+import torch
+import torch.distributed as dist
+import torch.distributed._symmetric_memory as symm_mem
+import torch.distributed.distributed_c10d as c10d
+
+
+logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)
+
+# GPU architectures the path is validated on.
+VALIDATED_ARCHS = ("gfx950",)
+MAX_CHUNKS = 16  # triggers per slot in the transport
+AUTO_MAX_CHUNKS = 8
+AUTO_MIN_PIECE_BYTES = 16 << 20
+MAX_WORLD = 64  # flag words one wait kernel checks
+ABI_VERSION = 3  # rsdma_abi_version of the transport this module calls
+DRAIN_S = 5.0  # how long an abandoned call's copies get to finish
+_EAGER_SLOTS = 4
+_CAPTURE_SLOTS = 8
+
+_lib = None
+_groups: dict[str, "_Group"] = {}
+_ipc_workspaces: dict[str, "_IpcWorkspace"] = {}
+_outgrown: list["_IpcWorkspace"] = []  # kept mapped: captured graphs may still use them
+_next_eager_slot = 0
+_next_capture_slot = 0
+_last_call = 0
+_broken: str | None = None  # why the transport can no longer be used
+_watchdog = None
+_warned_archs: set[str] = set()
+_warned_default_path = False
+
+# Calls that took this path, per op (for tests).
+num_calls = {
+    "fused_all_gather_matmul": 0,
+    "fused_matmul_reduce_scatter": 0,
+    "fused_all_gather_scaled_matmul": 0,
+    "fused_scaled_matmul_reduce_scatter": 0,
+}
+
+
+def _env(name: str, default: str) -> str:
+    return os.environ.get(f"TORCH_SYMM_MEM_{name}", default).strip()
+
+
+def _timeout_s() -> float:
+    return float(_env("ROCM_SDMA_TIMEOUT_S", "30"))
+
+
+def _on_timeout() -> str:
+    mode = _env("ROCM_SDMA_ON_TIMEOUT", "abort").lower()
+    if mode not in ("abort", "raise"):
+        raise ValueError(
+            f"TORCH_SYMM_MEM_ROCM_SDMA_ON_TIMEOUT must be abort or raise; got {mode!r}"
+        )
+    return mode
+
+
+def _inbox_mode() -> str:
+    mode = _env("ROCM_SDMA_INBOX", "ipc").lower()
+    if mode not in ("ipc", "symm_mem"):
+        raise ValueError(
+            f"TORCH_SYMM_MEM_ROCM_SDMA_INBOX must be ipc or symm_mem; got {mode!r}"
+        )
+    return mode
+
+
+def _arch(device: torch.device) -> str:
+    return torch.cuda.get_device_properties(device).gcnArchName.split(":")[0]
+
+
+def _check(rc: int, what: str) -> None:
+    if rc != 0:
+        raise RuntimeError(f"{what} failed with {rc}")
+
+
+def enabled() -> bool:
+    return torch.version.hip is not None and _env("ENABLE_ROCM_SDMA", "0") == "1"
+
+
+def _supported(t: torch.Tensor, row_dim: int, group_name: str) -> bool:
+    if (
+        not enabled()
+        or t.device.type != "cuda"
+        or t.dim() < 2
+        or not 0 <= row_dim < t.dim() - 1
+    ):
+        return False
+    if not 2 <= c10d._resolve_process_group(group_name).size() <= MAX_WORLD:
+        return False
+    arch = _arch(t.device)
+    if arch in VALIDATED_ARCHS or _env("ROCM_SDMA_ALLOW_UNTESTED", "0") == "1":
+        return True
+    if arch not in _warned_archs:
+        _warned_archs.add(arch)
+        logger.warning(
+            "symm_mem's SDMA path is validated on %s, not %s; using the default path. Set "
+            "TORCH_SYMM_MEM_ROCM_SDMA_ALLOW_UNTESTED=1 to use it anyway.",
+            ", ".join(VALIDATED_ARCHS),
+            arch,
+        )
+    return False
+
+
+def warn_default_path(op: str) -> None:
+    """Called when the path is enabled but `op` runs the default path: warn once that the default
+    path rendezvouses symmetric memory, which this path's ipc inbox avoids."""
+    global _warned_default_path
+    if _warned_default_path:
+        return
+    _warned_default_path = True
+    logger.warning(
+        "symm_mem's SDMA path does not support this %s call; it runs the default path, which "
+        "rendezvouses symmetric memory (on some amdgpu 6.x drivers this moves the memory to the "
+        "host). Warned once per process.",
+        op,
+    )
+
+
+def should_use_all_gather_matmul(
+    A_shard: torch.Tensor, Bs: list[torch.Tensor], gather_dim: int, group_name: str
+) -> bool:
+    """Whether fused_all_gather_matmul takes this path (other cases run the default one)."""
+    return all(B.dim() == 2 for B in Bs) and _supported(A_shard, gather_dim, group_name)
+
+
+def should_use_matmul_reduce_scatter(
+    A: torch.Tensor, B: torch.Tensor, reduce_op: str, scatter_dim: int, group_name: str
+) -> bool:
+    """Whether fused_matmul_reduce_scatter takes this path (other cases run the default one)."""
+    if (
+        B.dim() != 2
+        or reduce_op not in ("sum", "avg")
+        or not _supported(A, scatter_dim, group_name)
+    ):
+        return False
+    return A.shape[scatter_dim] % c10d._resolve_process_group(group_name).size() == 0
+
+
+def should_use_all_gather_scaled_matmul(
+    A_shard: torch.Tensor,
+    Bs: list[torch.Tensor],
+    A_scale: torch.Tensor,
+    gather_dim: int,
+    group_name: str,
+) -> bool:
+    """Whether fused_all_gather_scaled_matmul takes this path: tensor-wise, row-wise sharded and
+    row-wise replicated A scales (other cases run the default path)."""
+    if not should_use_all_gather_matmul(A_shard, Bs, gather_dim, group_name):
+        return False
+    world = c10d._resolve_process_group(group_name).size()
+    try:
+        symm_mem._check_and_verify_fp8_all_gather_scale_mode(
+            A_shard, A_scale, gather_dim, world
+        )
+    except ValueError:
+        return False  # the default path reports it
+    return True
+
+
+def should_use_scaled_matmul_reduce_scatter(
+    A: torch.Tensor,
+    B: torch.Tensor,
+    A_scale: torch.Tensor,
+    reduce_op: str,
+    orig_scatter_dim: int,
+    scatter_dim_after_maybe_reshape: int,
+    group_name: str,
+    output_shape: list[int],
+    out_dtype: torch.dtype | None,
+) -> bool:
+    """Whether fused_scaled_matmul_reduce_scatter takes this path: tensor-wise or row-wise A scales,
+    a bf16, fp16 or fp32 result (the partial sums are pushed in it), and each rank's output rows a
+    block of A's rows: A has the output's leading dims and the scatter dims agree, or A was
+    flattened from them and both scatter dims are 0 (other cases run the default path)."""
+    if out_dtype not in (torch.bfloat16, torch.float16, torch.float32):
+        return False
+    if A.dim() == len(output_shape) and list(A.shape[:-1]) == list(output_shape[:-1]):
+        if orig_scatter_dim != scatter_dim_after_maybe_reshape:
+            return False
+    elif orig_scatter_dim != 0 or scatter_dim_after_maybe_reshape != 0:
+        return False
+    if A_scale.numel() > 1 and (
+        A_scale.shape[:-1] != A.shape[:-1] or A_scale.shape[-1] != 1
+    ):
+        return False
+    if not should_use_matmul_reduce_scatter(
+        A, B, reduce_op, scatter_dim_after_maybe_reshape, group_name
+    ):
+        return False
+    world = c10d._resolve_process_group(group_name).size()
+    return output_shape[orig_scatter_dim] % world == 0
+
+
+def _load():
+    """Build (once, cached by torch.utils.cpp_extension) and load the transport."""
+    global _lib
+    if _lib is not None:
+        return _lib
+    from torch.utils import cpp_extension
+
+    source = Path(__file__).with_name("_rocm_sdma.hip")
+    # Named after the source, so a build of another version is never picked up.
+    digest = hashlib.sha256(source.read_bytes()).hexdigest()[:12]
+    path = cpp_extension.load(
+        name=f"torch_symm_mem_rocm_sdma_{digest}",
+        sources=[str(source)],
+        # In extra_cflags, where cpp_extension sees an explicit arch (else it builds for every visible GPU's).
+        extra_cflags=[
+            "-O2",
+            f"--offload-arch={_arch(torch.device('cuda', torch.cuda.current_device()))}",
+        ],
+        extra_ldflags=["-lhsa-runtime64"],
+        is_python_module=False,
+    )
+    lib = ctypes.CDLL(path)
+    lib.rsdma_abi_version.restype = ctypes.c_int
+    if lib.rsdma_abi_version() != ABI_VERSION:
+        raise RuntimeError(
+            f"{path} is SDMA transport version {lib.rsdma_abi_version()}, not {ABI_VERSION}"
+        )
+    i, u64, vp, dbl = ctypes.c_int, ctypes.c_uint64, ctypes.c_void_p, ctypes.c_double
+    ip, u64p = ctypes.POINTER(ctypes.c_int), ctypes.POINTER(ctypes.c_uint64)
+    for name, argtypes, restype in [
+        ("rsdma_init", [i, i], i),
+        ("rsdma_drain", [dbl, i], i),
+        ("rsdma_engine_plan", [i, ip, i, ip], i),
+        ("rsdma_plan_new", [i, i, i, i, dbl], vp),
+        ("rsdma_plan_push", [vp, i, u64p, u64p, u64p, ip, i, i, u64p], i),
+        ("rsdma_plan_run", [vp], i),
+        ("rsdma_plan_enqueue", [vp, vp], i),
+        ("rsdma_release", [i, i, vp], i),
+        ("rsdma_wait_flags", [vp, u64, i, dbl, i, i], i),
+        ("rsdma_peek_error", [ip, ip, ip, u64p], i),
+        ("rsdma_take_error", [ip, ip, ip, u64p], i),
+        ("rsdma_debug_drop_flag", [i, i], i),
+        ("rsdma_barrier", [vp, u64, u64, i, i, u64, dbl, i], i),
+        ("rsdma_ipc_alloc", [u64, ctypes.POINTER(vp), ctypes.c_char_p], i),
+        ("rsdma_ipc_open", [ctypes.c_char_p, ctypes.POINTER(vp)], i),
+    ]:
+        getattr(lib, name).argtypes = argtypes
+        getattr(lib, name).restype = restype
+    _lib = lib
+    atexit.register(lib.rsdma_drain, DRAIN_S, 0)
+    return lib
+
+
+def _ipc_share(lib, group, size: int) -> list[int]:
+    """`size` bytes of zeroed device memory on every rank of `group`, mapped in this process with
+    hipIpc handles: every rank's address here, in group rank order. Collective."""
+    ptr, handle = ctypes.c_void_p(), ctypes.create_string_buffer(64)
+    _check(lib.rsdma_ipc_alloc(size, ctypes.byref(ptr), handle), "rsdma_ipc_alloc")
+    handles = [None] * group.size()
+    dist.all_gather_object(handles, handle.raw, group=group)
+    bases = []
+    for r, h in enumerate(handles):
+        if r == group.rank():
+            bases.append(ptr.value)
+            continue
+        peer = ctypes.c_void_p()
+        _check(lib.rsdma_ipc_open(h, ctypes.byref(peer)), f"rsdma_ipc_open (rank {r})")
+        bases.append(peer.value)
+    return bases
+
+
+class _Group:
+    """Per process group: this rank's peers in step order, one SDMA engine per peer and a spare one,
+    and the arrival words of the ipc barrier."""
+
+    def __init__(self, group_name: str):
+        if torch.cuda.is_current_stream_capturing():
+            raise RuntimeError(
+                "symm_mem's SDMA path sets up a process group on its first call, which cannot be "
+                "captured: run the op once eagerly before capturing it"
+            )
+        lib = _load()
+        group = c10d._resolve_process_group(group_name)
+        self.rank, self.world = group.rank(), group.size()
+        device = torch.cuda.current_device()
+        devices = [None] * self.world
+        dist.all_gather_object(devices, device, group=group)
+        rc = lib.rsdma_init(device, _EAGER_SLOTS + _CAPTURE_SLOTS)
+        if rc == -11:
+            raise RuntimeError(
+                f"the SDMA transport has no GPU code for {_arch(torch.device('cuda', device))}"
+            )
+        _check(rc, "rsdma_init")
+        self.peers = [(self.rank + step) % self.world for step in range(1, self.world)]
+        n = len(self.peers)
+        peer_devs = (ctypes.c_int * n)(*[devices[p] for p in self.peers])
+        self.engine_arr = (ctypes.c_int * (n + 1))()
+        _check(
+            lib.rsdma_engine_plan(device, peer_devs, n, self.engine_arr),
+            "rsdma_engine_plan",
+        )
+        self.engines = list(self.engine_arr[:n])
+        # Per rank: `world` arrival words (word q: the last barrier epoch rank q reached), then the
+        # epoch word of its own barriers.
+        words = _ipc_share(lib, group, (self.world + 1) * 8)
+        self.arrivals = words[self.rank]
+        self.epoch = self.arrivals + self.world * 8
+        self.arrival_ptrs = torch.tensor(words, dtype=torch.int64, device=device)
+        _start_watchdog(lib)
+
+    def barrier(self, seconds: float) -> None:
+        """Enqueue on the current stream a barrier of the group's ranks, bounded by `seconds`; one
+        that runs out of time is reported as a failure of the current call."""
+        _check(
+            _load().rsdma_barrier(
+                ctypes.c_void_p(torch.cuda.current_stream().cuda_stream),
+                self.arrival_ptrs.data_ptr(),
+                self.arrivals,
+                self.world,
+                self.rank,
+                self.epoch,
+                seconds,
+                _last_call,
+            ),
+            "rsdma_barrier",
+        )
+
+
+def _group(group_name: str) -> _Group:
+    if group_name not in _groups:
+        _groups[group_name] = _Group(group_name)
+    return _groups[group_name]
+
+
+def engine_plan(group_name: str) -> dict:
+    """This rank's SDMA engines: {peer rank: engine}."""
+    g = _group(group_name)
+    return dict(zip(g.peers, g.engines))
+
+
+def debug_drop_flag(piece: int, peer_index: int) -> None:
+    """Test hook: the next issue of `piece` loses its flag write to peer index `peer_index`."""
+    _load().rsdma_debug_drop_flag(piece, peer_index)
+
+
+def _abandon(error: BaseException, ws, in_last_barrier: bool) -> None:
+    """After `error` stopped an eager call past its first barrier: let every copy of this process
+    finish now, so none is left waiting on a release that never comes, and peers waiting for this
+    call's flags see that it was abandoned and fail at once. Then, unless the call had reached it,
+    pass its last barrier, so peers waiting there are not held until it times out (a timed-out
+    barrier faults their GPU)."""
+    global _broken
+    pending = _load().rsdma_drain(DRAIN_S, 1)
+    if pending != 0:
+        _broken = (
+            f"an earlier call was abandoned ({type(error).__name__}) and its SDMA copies did not "
+            f"finish within {DRAIN_S:g} s ({pending})"
+        )
+        logger.error("symm_mem's SDMA path: %s", _broken)
+    if not in_last_barrier:
+        try:
+            _barrier(ws)
+        except Exception:
+            logger.exception("symm_mem's SDMA path: the abandoned call's last barrier failed")
+
+
+def _failure_message(
+    count: int, piece: int, call: int, status: int, missing: int
+) -> str:
+    rank = dist.get_rank() if dist.is_initialized() else "?"
+    plans = {name: dict(zip(g.peers, g.engines)) for name, g in _groups.items()}
+    if piece == -2:
+        ranks = [i for i in range(MAX_WORLD) if missing >> i & 1]
+        first = (
+            f"call {call}: group ranks {ranks} did not reach its barrier within "
+            f"{3 * _timeout_s():g} s"
+        )
+    elif status == 1:
+        words = [i for i in range(MAX_WORLD) if missing >> i & 1]
+        first = (
+            f"call {call}, piece {piece}: flag words {words} came from ranks that abandoned the "
+            "call (word r is group rank r's)"
+        )
+    elif status:
+        first = f"the host-function node of captured call {call} failed with {status}"
+    else:
+        words = [i for i in range(MAX_WORLD) if missing >> i & 1]
+        first = (
+            f"call {call}, piece {piece}: flag words {words} never set (word r is group rank r's) "
+            f"after {_timeout_s():g} s"
+        )
+    return f"rank {rank}: {count} symm_mem SDMA failure(s). First: {first}. SDMA engine per peer rank: {plans}"
+
+
+def _start_watchdog(lib) -> None:
+    """A thread that, in abort mode (read when it sees a failure), aborts the process once a flag
+    wait or a captured plan failed. In raise mode it leaves the failure to the next eager call."""
+    global _watchdog
+    if _watchdog is not None:
+        return
+
+    def watch():
+        piece, call, status, missing = (
+            ctypes.c_int(),
+            ctypes.c_int(),
+            ctypes.c_int(),
+            ctypes.c_uint64(),
+        )
+        while True:
+            count = lib.rsdma_peek_error(
+                ctypes.byref(piece),
+                ctypes.byref(call),
+                ctypes.byref(status),
+                ctypes.byref(missing),
+            )
+            if count and _on_timeout() == "abort":
+                message = _failure_message(
+                    count, piece.value, call.value, status.value, missing.value
+                )
+                logger.error("%s; aborting", message)
+                print(f"{message}; aborting", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
+                # No copy of this process is left waiting on the GPU once it is gone.
+                lib.rsdma_drain(DRAIN_S, 0)
+                os.abort()
+            time.sleep(0.1)
+
+    _watchdog = threading.Thread(
+        target=watch, name="symm-mem-rocm-sdma-watchdog", daemon=True
+    )
+    _watchdog.start()
+
+
+def raise_if_failed() -> None:
+    """Raise if a flag wait or captured plan of an earlier call failed (raise mode checks this every eager call)."""
+    piece, call, status, missing = (
+        ctypes.c_int(),
+        ctypes.c_int(),
+        ctypes.c_int(),
+        ctypes.c_uint64(),
+    )
+    count = _load().rsdma_take_error(
+        ctypes.byref(piece),
+        ctypes.byref(call),
+        ctypes.byref(status),
+        ctypes.byref(missing),
+    )
+    if count:
+        raise RuntimeError(
+            _failure_message(
+                count, piece.value, call.value, status.value, missing.value
+            )
+        )
+
+
+class _Plan:
+    """The host side of one call: its slot, call id and the pieces its SDMA engines push."""
+
+    def __init__(self, lib, g: _Group, pieces: int, copies_per_peer: int):
+        global _next_eager_slot, _next_capture_slot, _last_call
+        if _broken:
+            raise RuntimeError(f"symm_mem's SDMA path is unusable: {_broken}")
+        self.lib, self.g = lib, g
+        self.capturing = torch.cuda.is_current_stream_capturing()
+        if self.capturing:
+            self.slot = _EAGER_SLOTS + _next_capture_slot
+            _next_capture_slot = (_next_capture_slot + 1) % _CAPTURE_SLOTS
+        else:
+            if _on_timeout() == "raise":
+                raise_if_failed()
+            self.slot = _next_eager_slot
+            _next_eager_slot = (_next_eager_slot + 1) % _EAGER_SLOTS
+        _last_call += 1
+        self.call = _last_call
+        n = len(g.peers)
+        self.handle = lib.rsdma_plan_new(
+            self.slot, pieces * n * copies_per_peer, pieces * n, self.call, _timeout_s()
+        )
+        if not self.handle:
+            raise RuntimeError("rsdma_plan_new failed")
+
+    def push(
+        self,
+        k: int,
+        dst: list[int],
+        src: list[int],
+        nbytes: list[int],
+        flag_dst: list[int],
+    ) -> None:
+        """Add the next piece: for peer i (in g.peers order) and copy j, dst[i * m + j] <- src[i * m + j]
+        of nbytes[j] bytes, m = len(nbytes), released by trigger k; peer i's flag is written once
+        its m copies have landed."""
+        n, m = len(self.g.peers), len(nbytes)
+        u64 = ctypes.c_uint64
+        rc = self.lib.rsdma_plan_push(
+            self.handle,
+            k,
+            (u64 * (n * m))(*dst),
+            (u64 * (n * m))(*src),
+            (u64 * m)(*nbytes),
+            self.g.engine_arr,
+            n,
+            m,
+            (u64 * n)(*flag_dst),
+        )
+        _check(rc, "rsdma_plan_push")
+
+    def start(self, stream: torch.cuda.Stream) -> None:
+        """Issue the copies now, or when `stream` reaches this point on every replay if capturing."""
+        if self.capturing:
+            _check(
+                self.lib.rsdma_plan_enqueue(
+                    self.handle, ctypes.c_void_p(stream.cuda_stream)
+                ),
+                "rsdma_plan_enqueue",
+            )
+            return
+        rc = self.lib.rsdma_plan_run(self.handle)
+        n = len(self.g.peers)
+        if rc <= -2000:
+            raise RuntimeError(
+                f"flag write {-rc - 2000} of an earlier call on slot {self.slot} did not land "
+                f"within {_timeout_s():g} s"
+            )
+        if rc <= -1000:
+            i = -rc - 1000
+            raise RuntimeError(
+                f"a copy to peer rank {self.g.peers[i % n]} (SDMA engine {self.g.engines[i % n]}) of an earlier "
+                f"call on slot {self.slot} did not land within {_timeout_s():g} s"
+            )
+        _check(rc, "rsdma_plan_run")
+
+    def release(self, k: int, stream: torch.cuda.Stream) -> None:
+        """Let the pieces gated on trigger k start once `stream` reaches this point."""
+        _check(
+            self.lib.rsdma_release(self.slot, k, ctypes.c_void_p(stream.cuda_stream)),
+            "rsdma_release",
+        )
+
+    def wait(self, stream: torch.cuda.Stream, flags: torch.Tensor, piece: int) -> None:
+        """Make `stream` wait (bounded) until every int32 in `flags` reads 1. After a failure the
+        stream moves on; the watchdog aborts (abort mode) or the next eager call raises."""
+        rc = self.lib.rsdma_wait_flags(
+            ctypes.c_void_p(stream.cuda_stream),
+            flags.data_ptr(),
+            flags.numel(),
+            _timeout_s(),
+            piece,
+            self.call,
+        )
+        _check(rc, "rsdma_wait_flags")
+
+
+class _DeviceBytes:
+    def __init__(self, ptr: int, nbytes: int):
+        self.__cuda_array_interface__ = {
+            "shape": (nbytes,),
+            "typestr": "|u1",
+            "data": (ptr, False),
+            "version": 2,
+            "strides": None,
+        }
+
+
+class _IpcWorkspace:
+    """An ipc inbox: `size` bytes of device memory per rank of a group, mapped in every rank's
+    process (_ipc_share). Offers what _inbox and _barrier use of a symmetric-memory workspace."""
+
+    def __init__(self, group_name: str, size: int):
+        self.g = _group(group_name)
+        self.size = size
+        self.bases = _ipc_share(_load(), c10d._resolve_process_group(group_name), size)
+        self.device = torch.device("cuda", torch.cuda.current_device())
+        self._bytes: dict[int, torch.Tensor] = {}
+
+    def get_buffer(
+        self, rank: int, shape, dtype: torch.dtype, storage_offset: int = 0
+    ) -> torch.Tensor:
+        if rank not in self._bytes:
+            self._bytes[rank] = torch.as_tensor(
+                _DeviceBytes(self.bases[rank], self.size), device=self.device
+            )
+        start = storage_offset * dtype.itemsize
+        end = start + math.prod(shape) * dtype.itemsize
+        if end > self.size:
+            raise ValueError(f"bytes {start}..{end} exceed the {self.size}-byte inbox")
+        return self._bytes[rank][start:end].view(dtype).view(tuple(shape))
+
+    def barrier(self, channel: int = 0, timeout_ms: int = 0) -> None:
+        self.g.barrier(timeout_ms / 1000)
+
+
+def _ipc_workspace(group_name: str, min_size: int) -> _IpcWorkspace:
+    """As get_symm_mem_workspace, for the ipc inbox: grows to at least twice its size."""
+    ws = _ipc_workspaces.get(group_name)
+    if ws is not None and ws.size >= min_size:
+        return ws
+    if torch.cuda.is_current_stream_capturing():
+        raise RuntimeError(
+            f"symm_mem's SDMA path needs a {min_size}-byte inbox, larger than the "
+            f"{0 if ws is None else ws.size} bytes allocated, and cannot allocate it during "
+            "capture: run the op once eagerly with the captured shapes before capturing it"
+        )
+    size = max(min_size, 2 * ws.size) if ws is not None else min_size
+    if ws is not None:
+        _outgrown.append(ws)
+    ws = _ipc_workspaces[group_name] = _IpcWorkspace(group_name, -(-size // 64) * 64)
+    return ws
+
+
+def _inbox(group_name: str, rank: int, world: int, regions, chunks: int):
+    """This rank's inbox: one buffer per (shape, dtype) in `regions`, each 64-byte aligned, then
+    (chunks, world) int32 flag words. Also returns every rank's inbox base address and the byte
+    offsets of the regions and of the flags."""
+    offsets, size = [], 0
+    for shape, dtype in regions:
+        offsets.append(size)
+        nbytes = math.prod(shape) * dtype.itemsize
+        size += -(-nbytes // 64) * 64
+    flag_offset = size
+    size += chunks * world * 4
+    if _inbox_mode() == "ipc":
+        ws = _ipc_workspace(group_name, size)
+    else:
+        ws = symm_mem.get_symm_mem_workspace(group_name, min_size=size)
+    bufs = [
+        ws.get_buffer(rank, tuple(shape), dtype, storage_offset=offset // dtype.itemsize)
+        for (shape, dtype), offset in zip(regions, offsets)
+    ]
+    flags = ws.get_buffer(
+        rank, (chunks, world), torch.int32, storage_offset=flag_offset // 4
+    )
+    bases = [ws.get_buffer(r, (size,), torch.uint8).data_ptr() for r in range(world)]
+    return ws, bufs, offsets, flags, bases, flag_offset
+
+
+def _barrier(ws) -> None:
+    # A peer may reach the barrier only after waiting for its slot's previous copies and for its
+    # flags, each bounded by the timeout.
+    ws.barrier(channel=0, timeout_ms=int(_timeout_s() * 3 * 1000))
+
+
+def _chunks(rows: int, row_bytes: int) -> int:
+    """Pieces per rank for `rows` rows of `row_bytes` bytes each pushed per rank: the count set by
+    TORCH_SYMM_MEM_ROCM_SDMA_CHUNKS or picked from the piece size, lowered to divide `rows`."""
+    env = _env("ROCM_SDMA_CHUNKS", "")
+    if env:
+        want = int(env)
+    else:
+        fit = rows * row_bytes // AUTO_MIN_PIECE_BYTES
+        want = 1 << (min(max(fit, 1), AUTO_MAX_CHUNKS).bit_length() - 1)
+    if not 1 <= want <= MAX_CHUNKS:
+        raise ValueError(
+            f"TORCH_SYMM_MEM_ROCM_SDMA_CHUNKS must be 1 to {MAX_CHUNKS}; got {want}"
+        )
+    return max(c for c in range(1, want + 1) if rows % c == 0)
+
+
+def _aligned(scale: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
+    # As the default path: _scaled_mm's row-wise kernels need 16-byte aligned scales.
+    return scale if scale.data_ptr() % 16 == 0 else scale.clone()
+
+
+def _gather_rows(t: torch.Tensor, gather_dim: int, world: int):
+    """As _fused_all_gather_matmul_impl: `t` with gather_dim first, flattened to rows, and the
+    function that turns gathered rows back into the gathered tensor's shape."""
+    flat = t.movedim(gather_dim, 0)
+    leading_dims = [world] + list(flat.shape[:-1])
+
+    def unflatten(rows: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
+        return rows.view(*leading_dims, -1).flatten(0, 1).movedim(0, gather_dim)
+
+    return flat.flatten(0, -2), unflatten
+
+
+def _all_gather_and_consume(
+    tensors: list[torch.Tensor], chunks: int, group_name: str, consume, return_A: bool
+) -> torch.Tensor | None:
+    """Gathers every rank's rows of each (rows, features) tensor in `tensors` (A, then any per-row
+    data that goes with it, such as row-wise scales) into this rank's inbox, rank r's rows at
+    r * rows. Once piece c of every rank has landed, calls consume(c, pieces): pieces[j] is the
+    (world, block, features) piece c of tensors[j]. Returns the gathered tensors[0] if return_A."""
+    lib = _load()
+    g = _group(group_name)
+    world, rank = g.world, g.rank
+    rows = tensors[0].shape[0]
+    block = rows // chunks
+    stream = torch.cuda.current_stream()
+
+    # Region j of the inbox is the gathered tensors[j].
+    regions = [((world, rows, t.shape[1]), t.dtype) for t in tensors]
+    ws, inboxes, offsets, flags, bases, flag_offset = _inbox(
+        group_name, rank, world, regions, chunks
+    )
+    row_bytes = [t.shape[1] * t.element_size() for t in tensors]
+    plan = _Plan(lib, g, chunks, len(tensors))
+    for c in range(chunks):
+        # Piece c of this rank's rows, at the same offsets in every rank's inbox; the copies'
+        # source is this rank's own inbox.
+        at = [
+            offset + (rank * rows + c * block) * size
+            for offset, size in zip(offsets, row_bytes)
+        ]
+        plan.push(
+            0,
+            [bases[p] + a for p in g.peers for a in at],
+            [bases[rank] + a for _ in g.peers for a in at],
+            [block * size for size in row_bytes],
+            [bases[p] + flag_offset + (c * world + rank) * 4 for p in g.peers],
+        )
+    flags.zero_()
+    flags[:, rank] = 1
+    for inbox, t in zip(inboxes, tensors):
+        inbox[rank].copy_(t)
+
+    # Every rank's own rows and cleared flags are in place, and its inbox is free, past this barrier.
+    _barrier(ws)
+    # Issued after the kernels above are enqueued, so the GPU runs them meanwhile; the copies
+    # wait for the release.
+    in_last_barrier = False
+    try:
+        plan.start(stream)
+        plan.release(0, stream)
+        pieces = [inbox.view(world, chunks, block, -1) for inbox in inboxes]
+        for c in range(chunks):
+            plan.wait(stream, flags[c], c)
+            consume(c, [p[:, c] for p in pieces])
+        A = inboxes[0].reshape(world * rows, -1).clone() if return_A else None
+        # Every rank waited for every piece before its last matmul, so past this barrier no copy
+        # reads or writes this call's inboxes.
+        in_last_barrier = True
+        _barrier(ws)
+    except BaseException as e:
+        if not plan.capturing:
+            _abandon(e, ws, in_last_barrier)
+        raise
+    return A
+
+
+def _produce_and_reduce_scatter(
+    rows: int,
+    out_features: int,
+    dtype: torch.dtype,
+    chunks: int,
+    reduce_op: str,
+    group_name: str,
+    produce,
+) -> torch.Tensor:
+    """Reduce-scatter of a (world * rows, out_features) product that every rank holds a partial sum
+    of: owner r gets rows r * rows onward. produce(c, partials) writes this rank's partial sums for
